# Earflow Frontend (React)

## Stack

React 18, styled-components, framer-motion, react-router-dom v7, axios, hls.js. Build: CRACO (`npm start` / `npm run build`).

## Patterns

- Functional components + hooks; `memo()` for heavy player/queue components
- State: `PlayerContext`, `DeviceSyncContext`; auth via `useAuth`
- API: `api/client.js` — credentials included, CSRF from cookie
- Styles: colocated `ComponentName.styles.js`
- Runtime flags: `api/runtimeConfig.js` (e.g. `DEVICE_SYNC_ENABLED`)

## Player / streaming UI

- HLS: hls.js; stream sessions via `/api/stream/v2` or `/api/ebap-hls`
- Device Sync controls: `components/DeviceSync/`, `buildDeviceSyncControlDispatch`
- Do not bypass gateway for API calls in production paths

## Client UI preferences (mini bar / play button)

Read `.cursor/rules/earflow-ui-client-prefs.mdc` and `INV-FE-006..008` before changing `MobilePlayerBar`, `MiniBarVariantPicker`, `miniBarVariant.js`, `miniPlayStyle.js`.

- **Do:** `useSyncExternalStore` + `utils/*` store + `document.documentElement.dataset`.
- **Don't:** Profile-only `useState` without shared store; `apply*ToDom` (`INV-FE-007`).

## Avoid

- Storing tokens in localStorage/sessionStorage (JWT — `INV-SEC-001`; cosmetic UI prefs in localStorage are OK)
- Inline styles for complex layouts (use styled-components)
- Imperative DOM paint for UI prefs (`INV-FE-007`)
- Breaking mobile player layout constants (`MOBILE_CHROME_OFFSET_PX`, rail layout helpers)
